        {
            "timestamp": 1561563059,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Brad Bishop",
                "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                "username": "bradbishop"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 6:\n\n> Patch Set 6:\n> \n> Brad, IIRC, the ipmi-sensor and ipmi-fru are no longer supported via native recipes?  Or is it just that it's in transition?\n\nRight, I've been doing a lot of work to make expressing the IPMI YAML configuration simpler.  Could you have a look at how IPMI is configured in meta-ibm and restructure that way?\n\nIn a nutshell, you just need to bbappend the ipmi recipes and set DEPENDS and EXTRA_OECONF to point at a recipe that you host in your layer that provides the yaml files you want.  There is no need to have multiple recipes providing multiple yaml files (unless you want do do that) or set any preferred providers or anything like that."
        },
